//! flags: -b cuda

// A recursive exported function, compiled for CUDA.
//
// The CUDA backend works out which functions run on the host by walking the
// call graph from each exported one. The walk pushed a function's callees
// every time it reached that function, and never recorded where it had
// already been -- so a function that calls itself put itself back on the
// worklist for ever, and the compiler hung rather than failing. Sharing alone
// was enough to make it exponential; a cycle made it endless.
//
// Nothing about recursion is special to CUDA, and this is the smallest
// program that has a cycle in its call graph.
func [[export]] countdown(n : i32, acc : i32) -> i32 {
    if (n <= 0) {
        return acc;
    }
    return countdown(n - 1, acc + n);
}
